        "steps": [
          {
            "round": 5,
            "diary": "**Observations:** Price dipped to 99.5 in R1, recovered to 100 and flatlined for four rounds. My R3\u2013R4 buys filled at 100 (160 shares total, avg cost 100). My R5 order at limit 100.3 filled nothing \u2014 no momentum confirmation yet. Cash sits at ~$4,020. No news. **Beliefs:** I called this momentum shifting up after the dip was bought; so far it's just sideways. I'm underweight confidence \u2014 the tape hasn't agreed with me yet, but four flat holds at 100 still looks like accumulation to me. **Plan:** Don't force size until price breaks 100 with conviction. If it stalls, my conviction wavers fast \u2014 watch the next round closely.",
            "source_rounds": [
              1,
              2,
              3,
              4,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "round": 10,
            "diary": "**Observations:** Breakout to 100.6 filled me at 100.6 (round 7\u20138); I went all-in \u2014 200 shares, avg 100.11, cash $16. Then price fell to 98.6 and 98.1. Wealth down ~$480 over two rounds. No news. **Beliefs:** I called the 98.6 tick a shakeout \u2014 wrong so far. Momentum shifted down, not up. I overcommitted on a breakout that stalled instantly; my size, not my read of the dip, is the real error. I still think supply is thin, but I can't defend averaging in with $16. **Plan:** No cash to act. Hold and watch 98 \u2014 if it breaks, I'm riding 200 shares down without a hedge.",
            "source_rounds": [
              6,
              7,
              8,
              9,
              10
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
